findings.remediation:
Enforce a reasonable maximum length for the `upiId` string in the `submitWithdrawal` function. A limit of 100 characters, for example, would be sufficient for valid UPI IDs while preventing gas exhaustion attacks.

solidity
function submitWithdrawal(address user, uint256 amount, string calldata upiId) external onlyAuthorized {
    uint256 upiIdLength = bytes(upiId).length;
    require(upiIdLength > 0, "INRT: UPI ID cannot be empty");
    require(upiIdLength <= 100, "INRT: UPI ID too long");
    // ...
}

